## API Gateway Route Configuration

| Route | Auth | Streaming | Resource ID |
|-------|------|-----------|-------------|
| `GET /health` | NONE | BUFFERED | `yqy7it` |
| `POST /ai-chat` | COGNITO | STREAM | `qnq9v9` |
| `DELETE /ai-chat/{session_id}` | COGNITO | BUFFERED | `wj8vy2` |
| `GET /chat-room/messages/stream` | COGNITO | STREAM | `t3gp8c` |
| `POST /chat-room/messages` | COGNITO | BUFFERED | `inxjcr` |
| `GET /chat-room/messages` | NONE | BUFFERED | `inxjcr` |
| `POST /users/username` | COGNITO | BUFFERED | `pxb9gc` |
| `GET /users/me` | COGNITO | BUFFERED | `apa8gm` |
| `POST /metrics/{proxy+}` | NONE | BUFFERED | `xvam09` |

All routes also have OPTIONS methods as HTTP_PROXY pass-through (no auth) so FastAPI handles CORS preflight.

## CORS Strategy

CORS is handled by **FastAPI CORSMiddleware only** — API Gateway does NOT set CORS headers on successful responses. Gateway Responses (4xx/5xx errors generated by API Gateway itself) use `method.request.header.origin` to dynamically echo the request origin. Never add static multi-origin CORS headers in API Gateway.

## SSE Streaming

REST API (v1) supports `responseTransferMode: STREAM` with up to 15-minute duration and 5-minute idle timeout. This was chosen over HTTP API (v2) which has a hard 30-second integration timeout that kills SSE connections.

## Deploying Code Changes

```bash
# 1. Build and push new image
docker build -t uf-course-assistant ./UF-Course-Assistant
docker tag uf-course-assistant:latest 471112854227.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/uf-course-assistant:latest
docker push 471112854227.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/uf-course-assistant:latest

# 2. Force ECS to pull the new image
aws ecs update-service --cluster uf-scheduler-cluster --service uf-course-assistant-service --force-new-deployment

# 3. Monitor rollout
aws ecs describe-services --cluster uf-scheduler-cluster --services uf-course-assistant-service --query "services[0].{running:runningCount,desired:desiredCount,events:events[0:3]}"
```

## Secrets (SSM Parameter Store)

Secrets are injected as environment variables via ECS task definition `secrets` block. No AWS credentials are needed in the container — the ECS task IAM role provides DynamoDB access. Parameters live under `/uf-course-assistant/`:
- `OPENAI_API_KEY` (SecureString)
- `COGNITO_REGION`, `COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID`, `COGNITO_APP_CLIENT_ID`, `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` (String)

## Known Limitations

- **In-memory sessions**: `utils/sessions.py` stores AI chat sessions in process memory. Multiple ECS tasks will have isolated session stores. Needs Redis or DynamoDB for multi-task deployments.
- **In-memory pub/sub**: `api/controllers/chat_room.py` uses an in-process subscriber set. SSE clients connected to different tasks won't see each other's messages. Needs Redis pub/sub or DynamoDB Streams.
- **API Gateway stage prefix**: REST API prepends `/prod` to the path. The integration URI includes the full backend path so FastAPI sees the correct route.
